(: SMILE (PROMPT SYSTEM) SYNTAX :)
(-: Smile Window Host (-:
    (: What it does (:
        Any command line program, Claude Code included, opens as a draggable, resizable window in the Smile client, each with its own pseudo terminal.
        The Prompt to Sangha panel sets the network communication structure, writing style, roles, tools and sworn values, and sends one Smile prompt to every ticked window.
        Each prompt can carry a screenshot of the whole interface, saved under data/shots.
        Each window must reply with SMILE-ACK. A window whose output lacks it within twenty seconds receives the instruction again, up to two more times. Every spawn, prompt, followed and not-followed result goes to data/swarm-ledger.jsonl.
    :) thank you
    (: Start (:
        npm install, then node server.js, then open http://localhost:4444
    :) thank you
:-) End Smile Window Host :-) thank you
